I clicked Load once in a headless browser and the page never showed "Loaded 3 items". The result text stayed empty and there were no console errors.

The cause is in the page's `app.js` (lines 2–7). The click handler counts clicks and returns early on the first one (`if (clickCount === 1) return;`), so the text only appears on a second click. I didn't modify any files.

{"works": false, "cause": "The Load button's click handler in app.js ignores the first click, so 'Loaded 3 items' only appears after a second click."}
